(1358,'SM-240131-0005','dikirim via email dari yasmindignan@googlemail.com','UK Medical Student Elective','2024-01-30','2024-01-31','Direktur RSU. Bali Royal','1122','To whom it may concern, \r\n\r\nI am emailing to inquire into a UK medical student elective placement. We are four 4th Year Medical Students from the University of Bristol in the UK. The elective placement takes place from September to November, and we would be hoping to undertake a 2-4 week placement rotation in Indonesia. Would your hospital be able to accommodate this request? If needed we can provide letters of recommendations. Please can you let me know whether this would be possible - if so, what type of placements would be appropriate, how long and whether there are any necessary documents or insurance requirements. \r\n\r\nMany Thanks, \r\nYasmin Dignan\r\n',1,1,'2024-01-31 08:21:45','2024-02-01 03:35:10',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'Yanmed koordinasi dengan SDM dan Diklat untuk ditindaklanjuti','2024-02-01 03:35:10'),
(1359,'SM-240131-0006','dikirim melalui email ','Medical Elective - Bali Royal Hospital','2024-01-30','2024-01-31','Direktur RSU. Bali Royal','11334','Dear Bali Royal Hospital team,  \r\n \r\nI hope this email finds you well. My name is Manas Soni, and I am currently a fifth-year medical student. I am writing, alongside my colleague Neal Pun, to express our enthusiasm and keen interest in organising our elective at Bali Royal Hospital.  \r\n \r\nWe are particularly drawn to your hospital because of its reputation and its provision of a diverse and enriching learning environment. The opportunity to work alongside a multi-disciplinary team, including nurses, clinicians, and therapists, is something we find incredibly appealing. We believe that exposure to such a collaborative setting will significantly contribute to our overall medical education. \r\n  \r\nOur specific interest lies in a six-week elective opportunity (March 2025 – May 2025) within the emergency aspect of medicine, and we are excited about the prospect of learning from the experiences of your hospital\'s emergency services. Additionally, we are keen to explore the UDG and ICU/HDU services offered at Bali Royal Hospital. The chance to gain insights into these specialities within a setting which has received awards is particularly attractive to us.  \r\n \r\nWe understand that elective placements are highly competitive, and we want to assure you of our genuine enthusiasm and commitment to positively contributing to the Bali Royal Hospital during our elective period. We believe the exposure to your hospital\'s diverse medical services will significantly contribute to our medical training. We are fluent in English. Please let us know if this is suitable for the placement. We have also attached our CVs to this email.   \r\n \r\nIf needed, we are more than willing to provide any additional information or references that may support our application. We are prepared to comply with any application procedures your institution may have.  \r\nThank you for considering our application. We look forward to the possibility of undertaking our elective at Bali Royal Hospital and contributing to the valuable work conducted within your medical community.  \r\n \r\nWarm regards,  \r\nManas & Neal  \r\n',1,1,'2024-01-31 08:25:04','2024-02-01 03:35:50',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'Yanmed berkoordinasi dengan SDM dan Diklat untuk menindaklanjuti hal terkait','2024-02-01 03:35:50'),
